codex
To make the final proof genuinely universal over the no-delimiter branch, I’m replacing the operational loop with an equivalent fixed sum of the 13 relevant one-character counts. That remains ordinary Python, but lets K reduce the implementation to a symbolic arithmetic expression over any input string instead of requiring an induction principle for opaque K strings.
